`verilator_config
// [SPEC-TLP-06] The ingress raises a group's TX TVALID only in a clock where all its lanes have
// TREADY, and the shim's RX TREADY is its round on RX TVALID. Per lane neither TREADY (tile:
// sm_tx_ready && !wb_tx_wvalid) nor RX TVALID depends on the other side, so there is no bit-level
// loop; Verilator reports one because the tile computes ready, valid and the FIFO strobes of all
// lanes in one always_comb. UNOPTFLAT only costs simulation speed (Verilator iterates the block).
lint_off -rule UNOPTFLAT -file "*asp_pio_tile.sv" -match "*s_axis_tx_tvalid*"
lint_off -rule UNOPTFLAT -file "*asp_pio_tile.sv" -match "*m_axis_rx_tready*"
